# Copy to .env.local (gitignored) to override during development.

# --- API (server-side only: read by the Java backend in ../backend, never bundled) ---
# The backend reads this file when started on this machine (`../../scripts/dev.sh`);
# its own ../backend/.env.local, if there is one, wins. In production these are
# set in the Vercel project of the API (pulsarkids-api).
# Unset → the local Docker database (docker-compose.yml in the workspace folder, port 54329).
# The team setup points .env.local at the production (Neon) database.
# DATABASE_URL=postgres://wonderkids:wonderkids@localhost:54329/wonderkids
# Managed Postgres (Neon etc.): keep sslmode=require. PGSSL=true forces TLS.
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@HOST-pooler.REGION.aws.neon.tech/DBNAME?sslmode=require
# JWT_SECRET=dev-only-change-me
# JWT_EXPIRES_IN=30d

# Admin panel at /admin (accounts, progress, Google Speech per account).
# At least 8 characters (longer is safer); without it the admin API answers 503.
# ADMIN_KEY=change-me-to-a-long-random-string
# Encrypts stored Google API keys. Defaults to JWT_SECRET — if you set it, never
# change it later, or saved keys become unreadable.
# SECRETS_KEY=

# --- Letters from the site («Написати нам» → /admin/feedback) ---
# Every letter is stored in the database and forwarded to FEEDBACK_TO through
# Resend (https://resend.com), photos and videos attached — they are kept
# nowhere else. Without these two the text is still saved, but nothing is
# mailed and attached files are lost.
# RESEND_API_KEY=re_...
# FEEDBACK_TO=you@example.com
# The sender. Its domain must be verified in Resend (Domains → Add domain);
# until then only "Pulsar Kids <onboarding@resend.dev>" works, and only to the
# address the Resend account was registered with.
# FEEDBACK_FROM=Pulsar Kids <feedback@pulsarkids.com>

# --- Parent login through Auth0 (build time AND the API) ---
# Both values are public (Auth0 dashboard → Applications → your SPA → Settings).
# Set both to switch the parent login from email-only to Auth0; in Vercel add
# them for Production and Preview in BOTH projects — the game's (it builds with
# them) and the API's (it checks tokens with them) — then redeploy. Every origin a parent signs in
# on needs <origin>/parent-login in the application's Allowed Callback URLs and
# Allowed Logout URLs, and <origin> in Allowed Web Origins.
# VITE_AUTH0_DOMAIN=auth.pulsarkids.com
# VITE_AUTH0_CLIENT_ID=

# --- The public site (build time) ---
# The site is a deployment of its own (../site). The game only needs its
# address — the ROOT domain, no trailing slash — for the preview picture of its
# pages; the portals themselves are found by hostname (play.* / parents.*).
# VITE_SITE_URL=https://pulsarkids.com

# --- Where the API is ---
# On this machine the game's dev server passes /api on to the backend on port
# 4323. To ask another backend instead (shell variable, not this file):
#   VITE_API_TARGET=https://api.pulsarkids.com ../../scripts/dev.sh
# The production build calls the API at the api. subdomain of VITE_SITE_URL;
# set this only when the API has an address of its own.
# VITE_API_URL=https://api.pulsarkids.com
# The backend's own knobs (all optional): CORS_ORIGINS (root domains whose pages
# may call it, default pulsarkids.com,wonderkids.yluch.app), DB_POOL_MAX (5),
# PARENTS_URL (where a forwarded letter says the owner answers), OWNER_LANG (the
# language letters from the site are forwarded to you in: uk, en or pl; uk by default).

# Stripe — Family Pro billing (billing spec in ../doc). The API reads the secret
# key (sk_test_/rk_test_ in the sandbox, sk_live_/rk_live_ in production; a
# restricted key is better); without it billing is off. The publishable key is
# for the game's checkout later. The catalogue (products, prices, coupons, the
# customer portal) is made by `node ../scripts/stripe-setup.mjs`; the admin panel
# shows the connection in /admin/settings.
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_...
# VITE_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_test_...
